WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.430
This is the executive briefing
for AI Identity Governance,

3
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.874
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:11.710
It's for the people who make
the calls: the CIO, the CISO,

5
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:17.375
the Chief AI Officer, authorizing officials,
the privacy officer and sponsors.

6
00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:18.800
The argument is short.

7
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.875
An AI system that can act, not
just answer, is an account.

8
00:00:22.875 --> 00:00:28.013
Most AI arrived outside the identity
program, with no owner and no end date.

9
00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:30.449
And there's no separate AI authorization,

10
00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:35.537
so those accounts belong in the boundary
your authorizing official already reviews.

11
00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:38.775
I'll take four questions:
why, what, who and how.

12
00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:43.150
Each decision slide names the decision,
its owner and when it's needed.

13
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.580
Let's start with what
makes an agent an account.
